Subject: [PATCH] media_server: retry launching media_addon_server

_LaunchAddOnServer() tried be_roster->Launch() by MIME signature once,
fell back to a direct path launch once, and called exit(1) on the
whole media_server process if both failed -- confirmed as one of three
independent early-boot jobs (media_server, sshd, and the autologin job
that starts the user session in the first place -- see AGENTS.md) that
can lose a race against something still being readied elsewhere in the
system and exit immediately instead of hanging, with no further retry
since media_server is a `service` but exits fast enough each time that
nothing about it looks like a crash. Confirmed via launch_daemon's own
exit-status logging: media_server always exits with status 1 in a run
that never reaches a desktop, status 0 in one that does.

Wraps the existing signature-then-path launch attempt in a bounded
retry loop (up to 20 attempts, 100ms apart) instead of giving up
immediately. This does not by itself fully resolve the underlying race
(see AGENTS.md -- the same symptom can still outlast this retry
budget), but is a real, well-contained robustness fix in its own
right: media_server already tolerates this failure being transient
once (hence the signature-then-path fallback it already had), and
giving it more than one chance to clear a few hundred milliseconds of
boot jitter is strictly safer than exiting on the first failure.

diff --git a/src/servers/media/media_server.cpp b/src/servers/media/media_server.cpp
index 561eeec68a..6377f46940 100644
--- a/src/servers/media/media_server.cpp
+++ b/src/servers/media/media_server.cpp
@@ -190,30 +190,42 @@ ServerApp::ArgvReceived(int32 argc, char **argv)
 void
 ServerApp::_LaunchAddOnServer()
 {
-	// Try to launch media_addon_server by mime signature.
-	// If it fails (for example on the Live CD, where the executable
-	// hasn't yet been mimesetted), try from this application's
-	// directory
-	status_t err = be_roster->Launch(B_MEDIA_ADDON_SERVER_SIGNATURE);
-	if (err == B_OK)
-		return;
-
-	app_info info;
-	BEntry entry;
-	BDirectory dir;
-	entry_ref ref;
-
-	err = GetAppInfo(&info);
-	err |= entry.SetTo(&info.ref);
-	err |= entry.GetParent(&entry);
-	err |= dir.SetTo(&entry);
-	err |= entry.SetTo(&dir, "media_addon_server");
-	err |= entry.GetRef(&ref);
-
-	if (err == B_OK)
-		be_roster->Launch(&ref);
-	if (err == B_OK)
-		return;
+	// Try to launch media_addon_server by mime signature. If it fails (for
+	// example on the Live CD, where the executable hasn't yet been
+	// mimesetted, or early at boot, where the registrar's MIME database and
+	// app list may not be fully populated yet), try from this application's
+	// directory. Retry both for a few seconds before giving up: this is a
+	// one-time startup race, not a hard dependency failure, and giving up on
+	// the first attempt turned media_server into the most eager thing to
+	// fail during a boot that's merely running a little behind (confirmed
+	// under QEMU with a NIC attached, where other early boot steps can push
+	// this race just far enough to lose).
+	status_t err = B_ERROR;
+	for (int attempt = 0; attempt < 20; attempt++) {
+		if (attempt > 0)
+			snooze(100000);
+
+		err = be_roster->Launch(B_MEDIA_ADDON_SERVER_SIGNATURE);
+		if (err == B_OK)
+			return;
+
+		app_info info;
+		BEntry entry;
+		BDirectory dir;
+		entry_ref ref;
+
+		err = GetAppInfo(&info);
+		err |= entry.SetTo(&info.ref);
+		err |= entry.GetParent(&entry);
+		err |= dir.SetTo(&entry);
+		err |= entry.SetTo(&dir, "media_addon_server");
+		err |= entry.GetRef(&ref);
+
+		if (err == B_OK)
+			err = be_roster->Launch(&ref);
+		if (err == B_OK)
+			return;
+	}

 	BAlert* alert = new BAlert("media_server", "Launching media_addon_server "
 		"failed.\n\nmedia_server will terminate", "OK");
